.TH NPA 1 "2026-06-17" "npa 0.1.0" "Network Packet Analyzer"
.SH NAME
npa \- terminal network packet analyzer with anomaly detection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B npa
.RB [ \-i
.IR iface " | " \-r
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR bpf ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-headless ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-count
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-rules
.IR file ]
.RB [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B npa
is a Wireshark\-lite tool for live capture, protocol decoding (Ethernet/802.1Q,
IPv4, IPv6, TCP, UDP, ICMP/ICMPv6), and rule\-driven anomaly detection, rendered
in an ncurses TUI. It can also read offline pcap files and run headless for
scripting and CI.
.PP
Capturing live traffic requires raw\-socket privileges. Prefer file capabilities
over running as root:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo setcap cap_net_raw,cap_net_admin+eip /usr/local/bin/npa
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Source (choose one)
.TP
.BI \-i " iface" "\fR, \fP" \-\-interface " iface"
Capture live on the given network interface.
.TP
.BI \-r " file" "\fR, \fP" \-\-read " file"
Read packets from a pcap file instead of a live interface.
.SS Capture
.TP
.BI \-f " bpf" "\fR, \fP" \-\-filter " bpf"
Apply a Berkeley Packet Filter expression (e.g. "tcp port 443").
.TP
.BI \-s " n" "\fR, \fP" \-\-snaplen " n"
Bytes captured per packet (default 65535).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-no\-promisc
Disable promiscuous mode.
.TP
.BI \-w " file" "\fR, \fP" \-\-write " file"
Tee every captured packet to a pcap file (full fidelity).
.SS Pipeline
.TP
.BI \-\-ring\-size " n"
Ring buffer slots, rounded up to a power of two (default 1024).
.TP
.B \-\-block
Block the capture thread when the ring is full instead of dropping.
.SS Detection / UI
.TP
.BI \-\-rules " file"
Load anomaly rules from a file (merged over the built\-ins, by name).
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without the ncurses UI (scripting / CI).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Headless: emit JSON Lines (alerts + a final summary) on stdout. Implies
.BR \-\-headless .
.TP
.BI \-\-count " n"
Stop after analyzing N packets (0 = unlimited).
.TP
.BI \-\-stats\-interval " s"
Headless: print a stats line every S seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " path"
Write logs to a file (default: stderr). Logs never go to stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
One of trace, debug, info, warn, error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH "INTERACTIVE KEYS"
.TP
.BR Up / Down
Move the packet selection.
.TP
.BR PgUp / PgDn ", " Home / End
Scroll the packet list.
.TP
.B p
Freeze / resume the live list (stats keep updating).
.TP
.B /
Prompt for a new BPF filter and apply it live.
.TP
.B w
Export retained packets to a timestamped pcap.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings resolve in order (later wins): built\-in defaults,
.IR /etc/npa/npa.conf ", " ./npa.conf ", " $NPA_* " environment variables,"
then command\-line flags. See
.I npa.conf.example
and
.IR patterns.rules .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Live capture on eth0, HTTPS only:
.B npa \-i eth0 \-f "tcp port 443"
.TP
Offline analysis, machine\-readable:
.B npa \-r capture.pcap \-\-headless \-\-json
.TP
Capture to disk while analyzing:
.B npa \-i eth0 \-w out.pcap
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 on a usage/configuration error, 1 on a runtime failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR wireshark (1),
.BR pcap (3PCAP)
.SH AUTHORS
Network Packet Analyzer contributors.
